  "root_cause_analysis": {
    "summary": "Attacker-controlled Spinel on-mesh-prefix data drives wpantund prefix/address state updates. A matching SLAAC unicast address is stored in mUnicastAddresses. During prefix removal, on_mesh_prefix_was_removed finds the address entry and binds address as a const reference to addr_iter->first. It then calls unicast_address_was_removed with that reference; the callee erases the same mUnicastAddresses entry and then passes &address to TunnelIPv6Interface::remove_address. Since address still refers to the erased map key, remove_address reads freed storage and ASan reports a heap-use-after-free.",
    "key_mechanism": "reference_to_map_key_used_after_erase",
    "why_patch_works": "The patch changes address from a const reference to a by-value struct in6_addr copy. The copy remains valid even after mUnicastAddresses.erase removes the original map node, so later remove_address receives a pointer to live stack storage and the fixed build no longer crashes."
  },
